Test_ID,Title,Description,Preconditions,Steps,Expected_Result,Type,Owner,Priority,Coverage_Goal,Environment,Seeds,Regression_Suite,References
TP_GPIO_001,GPIO Register Read/Write Sanity,Verify basic read/write access for all primary GPIO registers (DIR, DATA_OUT, DATA_IN, INT_EN, INT_TYPE, INT_POL, INT_STATUS/CLEAR, PAD_EN, SW_RESET) without using macros.,SoC powered; GPIO clock enabled; GPIO base address mapped.,1) Deassert GPIO_SW_RESET. 2) Write legal values to GPIO_DIR and read back. 3) Write walking-1s to GPIO_DATA_OUT and sample on GPIO_DATA_IN via loopback. 4) Enable bits in GPIO_INT_EN with INT_TYPE=level and INT_POL=active-high then clear via GPIO_INT_CLEAR. 5) Toggle GPIO_PAD_EN to validate pad gating.,All register writes/readbacks match; DATA_IN reflects DATA_OUT when loopback is present; INT_STATUS sets and is cleared by GPIO_INT_CLEAR; No bus errors.,Sanity,PSVValidation,P0,Access + basic functional coverage across all pads and interrupt enables,Baremetal on PSV target; GCC; on-board loopback or harness,0x1,GPIO_Smoke,https://github.com/titusbspgit/PSVValidation/tree/main/TestRepo/gpio/gpio_reg_wr_rd_test
TP_GPIO_002,Negative Edge Interrupt Enable,Validate interrupt generation on negative edge when GPIO_INT_TYPE=edge and GPIO_INT_POL=negative.,GPIO lines connected to pattern generator or loopback; NVIC configured if applicable.,1) Set GPIO_DIR for target pins as input. 2) Program GPIO_INT_TYPE=edge. 3) Program GPIO_INT_POL=neg. 4) Enable target bits in GPIO_INT_EN. 5) Drive high-to-low transitions on enabled pads. 6) Read GPIO_INT_STATUS and clear via GPIO_INT_CLEAR.,Interrupt triggers per enabled pad on falling edges; status bits set and cleared; no spurious on other pads.,Interrupt,PSVValidation,P0,Edge polarity coverage across all pads,Baremetal on PSV target; pattern gen or GPIO toggle from peer,0x2,GPIO_Edge,https://github.com/titusbspgit/PSVValidation/tree/main/TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_negedge_intr_en
TP_GPIO_003,Positive Edge Interrupt Enable,Validate interrupt generation on positive edge.,Same as TP_GPIO_002.,1) Set inputs. 2) INT_TYPE=edge. 3) INT_POL=pos. 4) Enable INT_EN bits. 5) Drive low-to-high transitions. 6) Check INT_STATUS and clear.,Interrupt triggers per enabled pad on rising edges; clean clear.,Interrupt,PSVValidation,P0,Edge polarity coverage across all pads,Baremetal on PSV target,0x3,GPIO_Edge,https://github.com/titusbspgit/PSVValidation/tree/main/TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_posedge_intr_en
TP_GPIO_004,Both-Edge Interrupt Enable,Validate both-edge interrupt behavior when both positive and negative edges are intended (if supported via INT_BOTH or by sequence).,Same as TP_GPIO_002.,1) Configure as inputs. 2) If GPIO supports both-edge: set INT_TYPE=edge and enable both-edge mode; else alternate INT_POL and verify each edge. 3) Enable INT_EN. 4) Apply toggling stimulus.,Interrupt fires on both transitions; no double-counting or missed events.,Interrupt,PSVValidation,P1,Both-edge functional coverage,Baremetal on PSV target,0x4,GPIO_Edge,https://github.com/titusbspgit/PSVValidation/tree/main/TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_pos_neg_intr_en
TP_GPIO_005,Level-Select Interrupt Enable,Validate level-sensitive interrupts with GPIO_INT_TYPE=level and both polarities via GPIO_INT_POL.,Same as TP_GPIO_002.,1) Inputs mode. 2) INT_TYPE=level. 3) INT_POL=high; drive high level; verify latch and clear. 4) INT_POL=low; drive low level; verify.,Level interrupts latch while asserted and clear when deasserted and written to GPIO_INT_CLEAR.,Interrupt,PSVValidation,P0,Level vs edge mode coverage,Baremetal on PSV target,0x5,GPIO_Level,https://github.com/titusbspgit/PSVValidation/tree/main/TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en
TP_GPIO_006,Operation Mode - All Pads Enable,Validate GPIO operation when all pads are enabled via GPIO_PAD_EN and correctly driven/read.,SoC init complete.,1) Set GPIO_PAD_EN=all. 2) Alternate GPIO_DIR between output and input tests. 3) For outputs drive patterns on GPIO_DATA_OUT; for inputs sample GPIO_DATA_IN.,All pads respond per configuration with no contention when switching modes.,Functional,PSVValidation,P1,Pad enable functional coverage,Baremetal on PSV target,0x6,GPIO_Mode,https://github.com/titusbspgit/PSVValidation/tree/main/TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_op_mode_all_pad_en
TP_GPIO_007,Output Mode Test,Validate output drive via GPIO_DATA_OUT with corresponding GPIO_DIR settings.,Loopback or measurement instrumentation available.,1) Set GPIO_DIR=outputs for selected pads. 2) Drive pattern sequence on GPIO_DATA_OUT. 3) Observe via loopback or probe.,Driven values match expected; no glitches during static writes.,Functional,PSVValidation,P1,Output drive functional coverage,Baremetal on PSV target,0x7,GPIO_Mode,https://github.com/titusbspgit/PSVValidation/tree/main/TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_output_mode_test
TP_GPIO_008,Negedge - All Pads Enabled,Validate negedge interrupt on all pads enabled.,As in TP_GPIO_002.,1) INT_TYPE=edge; INT_POL=neg; INT_EN=all pads; 2) Sweep falling transitions per pad.,Each pad triggers exactly once per falling edge; status clears.,Interrupt,PSVValidation,P1,Pad-wise edge coverage,Baremetal on PSV target,0x8,GPIO_Edge,https://github.com/titusbspgit/PSVValidation/tree/main/TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_negedge_all_pads_en
TP_GPIO_009,Pedge - All Pads Enabled,Validate posedge interrupt on all pads enabled.,As in TP_GPIO_003.,1) INT_TYPE=edge; INT_POL=pos; INT_EN=all pads; 2) Sweep rising transitions per pad.,Each pad triggers exactly once per rising edge; status clears.,Interrupt,PSVValidation,P1,Pad-wise edge coverage,Baremetal on PSV target,0x9,GPIO_Edge,https://github.com/titusbspgit/PSVValidation/tree/main/TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_pedge_all_pads_en
